---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import SocialMeta from "../components/SocialMeta.astro";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="any" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Terms of Use — Nail Bite Beaver</title>
    <SocialMeta
      title="Terms of Use — Nail Bite Beaver"
      description="Terms of Use for Nail Bite Beaver. Must be of legal age. Camera monitoring and on-screen reminders are used at your own judgment. Refunds available if it doesn't work on your supported Mac."
      path="/terms"
    />

    <!-- Google tag (gtag.js) -->
    <script async src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtag/js?id=G-DM7ZR8WCHR"
    ></script>
    <script is:inline>
      window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
      function gtag() {
        dataLayer.push(arguments);
      }
      gtag("js", new Date());
      gtag("config", "G-DM7ZR8WCHR");

      /**
       * Fire a custom GA4 event.
       * @param {string} eventName
       * @param {Record<string, string | number | boolean>} [params]
       */
      function trackEvent(eventName, params) {
        gtag("event", eventName, params);
      }
    </script>

    <style>
      @import url("https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Nunito:wght@500;600;700;800&display=swap");

      html,
      body {
        overflow-x: hidden;
      }

      body {
        background: #f6ebda;
        color: #2c3e50;
        font-family: "Nunito", system-ui, sans-serif;
        font-weight: 500;
        margin: 0;
      }

      h1,
      h2,
      h3,
      strong {
        font-weight: 800;
      }

      a {
        color: #2c3e50;
      }

      a:hover,
      a:focus-visible {
        color: #c1763d;
      }

      .page {
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 5rem;
      }

      .back-bar {
        position: fixed;
        top: 0;
        left: 0;
        right: 0;
        z-index: 10;
        background: #f6ebda;
      }

      .back-bar__inner {
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
      }

      .back-link {
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        text-underline-offset: 4px;
      }

      .page h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 2.75rem);
        line-height: 1.15;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }

      .updated {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.875rem;
        color: #5a6b7a;
      }

      .tldr {
        margin: 2rem 0 0;
        padding: 1.25rem 1.35rem;
        border-radius: 12px;
        background: rgba(193, 118, 61, 0.12);
        border: 1px solid rgba(193, 118, 61, 0.35);
      }

      .tldr__label {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #c1763d;
      }

      .tldr p {
        margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: #2c3e50;
      }

      .policy-section {
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
      }

      .policy-section h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }

      .policy-section p,
      .policy-section li {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.65;
        color: #5a6b7a;
      }

      .policy-section p {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
      }

      .policy-section ul {
        margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
        padding-left: 1.25rem;
      }

      .policy-section li + li {
        margin-top: 0.45rem;
      }

      .policy-section a {
        font-weight: 700;
        text-underline-offset: 4px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="back-bar">
      <div class="back-bar__inner">
        <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to home</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <main class="page">
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: September 30, 2026</p>

      <aside class="tldr">
        <p class="tldr__label">TL;DR</p>
        <p>
          Must be of legal age in your jurisdiction to use. Nail Bite Beaver
          watches your webcam on-device and may pop a beaver over your screen
          when it thinks you’re biting your nails or touching your face. That
          can interrupt meetings, games, or focus — if that gets awkward, that’s
          on you. Detection isn’t perfect. This isn’t medical advice or a
          guaranteed cure for nail-biting. If the app doesn’t work as expected
          on a supported Mac, email{" "}
          <a href="mailto:support@nailbitebeaver.com"
            >support@nailbitebeaver.com</a
          >{" "}
          and we’ll help or refund you.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By downloading, installing, or using Nail Bite Beaver ("the
          Software"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Use. If you do not
          agree to these terms, do not use the Software.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>2. Age Requirement</h2>
        <p>
          You must be of legal age in your jurisdiction to use Nail Bite Beaver.
          By purchasing or using the Software, you confirm that you meet the
          minimum age requirement under applicable law in your country or
          region. The developer assumes no responsibility for use of the
          Software by minors and disclaims all liability arising from underage
          access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>3. Description of the Software</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver is a novelty macOS application that uses your Mac’s
          camera to detect nail-biting or hand-to-face movement on-device, then
          shows an on-screen beaver reminder — including overlays that may
          briefly cover part or all of your display. The Software is provided as
          a personal habit reminder and entertainment tool. It is not, and is
          not represented to be, a medical device, clinical treatment, therapy,
          or guaranteed cure for nail-biting or related behaviors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>4. Camera &amp; Detection Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>You use Nail Bite Beaver entirely at your own risk.</strong>{" "}
          The Software requires camera access and continuously samples video
          frames while monitoring is enabled. Detection is heuristic and
          imperfect. The Software may:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Miss real nail-biting or hand-to-face behavior (false negatives)</li>
          <li>
            Trigger when you are not biting your nails — for example while
            eating, resting your chin, adjusting glasses, applying makeup, or
            gesturing near your face (false positives)
          </li>
          <li>
            Interrupt your screen during video calls, presentations, gaming, or
            other focused work when an overlay appears
          </li>
          <li>
            Use additional CPU, GPU, Neural Engine, and battery while the camera
            and on-device models are active
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          You are solely responsible for deciding when monitoring is appropriate,
          for pausing or quitting the Software when an interruption would be
          harmful or inappropriate, and for any consequence of a missed or
          incorrect detection.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>5. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the developer shall
          not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, or punitive damages arising out of or in connection
          with your use of the Software, including but not limited to damages
          for loss of profits, data, goodwill, productivity, or other intangible
          losses, even if the developer has been advised of the possibility of
          such damages.
        </p>
        <p>
          In no event shall the developer's total liability exceed the amount
          you paid for the Software.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>6. No Warranty</h2>
        <p>
          The Software is provided "as is" and "as available" without warranties
          of any kind, either express or implied, including but not limited to
          implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
          purpose, and non-infringement. The developer does not warrant that the
          Software will be uninterrupted, error-free, accurate in every
          detection, or free of harmful components.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>7. Assumption of Risk</h2>
        <p>
          You expressly acknowledge and agree that use of the Software involves
          continuous camera monitoring and on-screen interruptions. You assume
          all risk of embarrassment, disruption, missed work, or loss that may
          result from using the Software as intended or otherwise.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>8. Disclaimer of Liability for Social and Professional Consequences</h2>
        <p>
          The developer shall not be held liable for any social, professional,
          reputational, or personal consequences arising from the use of the
          Software in any setting, including but not limited to workplaces,
          educational institutions, public spaces, video calls, streams, or
          private gatherings. Without limiting the generality of the foregoing,
          the developer expressly disclaims responsibility for any adverse
          outcomes including but not limited to termination of employment,
          disciplinary action, loss of professional standing, damage to personal
          or business relationships, ejection from premises, or public
          embarrassment resulting from the beaver overlay, detection alerts, or
          other visual effects produced by the Software. You acknowledge that
          you are solely responsible for exercising appropriate judgment
          regarding when, where, and in whose presence you choose to operate the
          Software.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>9. Lawful Use of the Camera</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to use the Software only on devices you own or are expressly
          authorized to use, and only in a manner consistent with all applicable
          laws and regulations governing cameras, workplace monitoring, and
          privacy. You are solely responsible for ensuring that running the
          Software (including facing a webcam toward yourself or others nearby)
          is lawful in your location and setting. The developer is not
          responsible for unlawful use and you agree to indemnify the developer
          in accordance with Section 10.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>10. Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the developer from
          and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses
          (including reasonable legal fees) arising out of or related to your
          use of the Software or violation of these Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>11. License</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver grants you a personal, non-transferable,
          non-exclusive, revocable license to use the Software on devices you
          own or control, subject to a valid license obtained through our
          authorized payment provider (Lemon Squeezy) or the Mac App Store, as
          applicable. You may not redistribute, reverse-engineer, decompile, or
          create derivative works based on the Software, except to the extent
          such restriction is prohibited by applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>12. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>
          The Nail Bite Beaver name, logo, beaver artwork, brand colors, visual
          design, website content, and all associated materials are the
          exclusive intellectual property of the developer. All rights not
          expressly granted in these Terms are reserved.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may not copy, reproduce, imitate, or create derivative works of
          the Nail Bite Beaver brand identity, including but not limited to the
          logo, beaver character, color scheme, website design, or marketing
          materials, without prior written consent from the developer.
          Unauthorized use of any Nail Bite Beaver intellectual property will be
          pursued to the fullest extent of applicable law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>13. Open Source Acknowledgments</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver incorporates open source components, including
          Sparkle (used for update checks on direct downloads). Full license
          texts for bundled open source components are included with the
          Software distribution where required. The use of these components does
          not imply endorsement by their respective authors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>14. Refund Policy</h2>
        <p>
          If the Software fails to function on your supported device, email us
          at{" "}
          <a href="mailto:support@nailbitebeaver.com"
            >support@nailbitebeaver.com</a
          >{" "}
          and we will work to resolve the issue or provide a refund. We might
          ask for a short video or screenshot showing the issue to help
          diagnose the problem.
        </p>
        <p>
          Separately, promotional refunds or discounts for posting Reels are
          governed by the offer terms described on the{" "}
          <a href="/discount">discount page</a>. Those promotions may end at any
          time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>15. System Requirements</h2>
        <p>
          Nail Bite Beaver requires macOS 15 (Sequoia) or later and a Mac with a
          working camera. Apple Silicon is recommended. The developer is not
          responsible for issues arising from use on unsupported hardware,
          operating system versions, or devices without a functioning camera and
          camera permission.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>16. Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Camera frames are processed on your Mac and are not uploaded by the
          Software. License validation and (on direct downloads) update checks
          may involve limited network requests. For full details, see our{" "}
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>17. Marketing Communications</h2>
        <p>
          When you purchase Nail Bite Beaver, your email address is collected as
          part of the transaction (via Lemon Squeezy or the Mac App Store, as
          applicable). By completing a purchase and not requesting a refund, you
          agree that the developer may use your email address to send occasional
          marketing communications, including but not limited to product
          updates, new features, promotions, and related announcements.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every marketing email will include a clear and easy way to unsubscribe.
          Once you unsubscribe, you will no longer receive marketing emails,
          though you may still receive transactional emails related to your
          purchase (e.g., refund confirmations or license recovery).
        </p>
        <p>
          The developer will not sell, rent, or share your email address with
          third parties for their own marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>18. Changes to These Terms</h2>
        <p>
          The developer reserves the right to modify these Terms at any time.
          Changes will be reflected on this page with an updated date. Continued
          use of the Software after changes constitutes acceptance of the
          updated Terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>19. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the
          laws of the jurisdiction in which the developer resides, without
          regard to conflict of law principles.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="policy-section">
        <h2>20. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For questions about these Terms, contact us at{" "}
          <a href="mailto:support@nailbitebeaver.com"
            >support@nailbitebeaver.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />

    <script is:inline>
      document.querySelector(".back-link")?.addEventListener("click", () => {
        trackEvent("terms_back_click");
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
